{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792508758701,"sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"todowrite","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9eb36308a7ae1a06","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"todos":[{"content":"Write correctness-first dynamic DFS candidate (keep-or-rebuild)","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run checks (<=8) to reach full correctness at search level","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Reduce work_ratio (avoid full recompute) if room remains","status":"pending","priority":"medium"},{"content":"Run final check and evoalgo finish","status":"pending","priority":"high"}]},"output":"[\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Write correctness-first dynamic DFS candidate (keep-or-rebuild)\",\n    \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Run checks (<=8) to reach full correctness at search level\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Reduce work_ratio (avoid full recompute) if room remains\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Run final check and evoalgo finish\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  }\n]","metadata":{"todos":[{"content":"Write correctness-first dynamic DFS candidate (keep-or-rebuild)","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run checks (<=8) to reach full correctness at search level","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Reduce work_ratio (avoid full recompute) if room remains","status":"pending","priority":"medium"},{"content":"Run final check and evoalgo finish","status":"pending","priority":"high"}],"truncated":false},"title":"4 todos","time":{"start":1792508758667,"end":1792508758685}},"id":"prt_159d907870017xpO0YQk3J8dTr","sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","messageID":"msg_159d6f62a0017s4ZTYfD5pre09"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1792508758702,"sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","part":{"id":"prt_159d8fc01001Pm4Zgjm2qUuUgo","messageID":"msg_159d6f62a0017s4ZTYfD5pre09","sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","type":"text","text":"\n\nI now understand the problem, the verifier's invariant, and how work is measured. Let me set up my plan and write the candidate.\n\nKey facts I verified:\n- **State contract**: dict with `parent`, `discover`, `finish`. The checker (`_verify_dfs_certificate`) requires: root has no parent + is discovered; every reachable vertex is discovered; each reachable non-root `v` has a parent that is a neighbor discovered before it; and **no forward-cross edge** (for every edge `u->v` with `discover[u] < discover[v]`, `v` must be a descendant of `u`).\n- **Crucial**: the parent edge is itself checked by the no-forward-cross rule, so a parent must actually be an *ancestor*. Stale (now-unreachable) vertices are **not** checked.\n- **work_ratio** = candidate wall-time / offline-DFS wall-time, so I must avoid full recomputes on most updates.\n\nMy algorithm exploits that a single edge flip only affects validity locally:\n- **Insert `u->v`**: breaks the forest only if it makes a new vertex reachable, or is a forward-cross edge.\n- **Delete `u->v`**: breaks the forest only if `u->v` is a tree edge (`parent[v]==u`), dangling `v`'s parent. Deletions never create a forward-cross edge, and a deleted non-tree edge leaves every vertex reachable via its tree path.\n\nOtherwise the existing forest is still valid and is returned unchanged.\n\n","time":{"start":1792508754946,"end":1792508758692}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1792508759048,"sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","part":{"id":"prt_159d90bf60016F5DSQcRx0Z6Az","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"2930e359069e09b812cf99cf8e4b01c9af39c2f0","messageID":"msg_159d6f62a0017s4ZTYfD5pre09","sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":78148,"input":54587,"output":469,"reasoning":23092,"cache":{"write":0,"read":0}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1792508760122,"sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","part":{"id":"prt_159d9100b001Psg1P4z56seEwz","messageID":"msg_159d90cf80015oGi2PyLyKCLJK","sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","snapshot":"4297cad3ba4338abbb70ddd3660449cb7424f17d","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792508766003,"sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8c1baf4b8d54adde","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s2/candidate.py","content":"\"\"\"Dynamic DFS forest maintenance (directed, root 0).\n\nA single edge flip only invalidates the maintained DFS forest in a local way,\nso most updates are answered by keeping the existing forest untouched:\n\n- Insert u->v: the old forest is still a DFS forest unless the new edge\n  (a) makes a previously unreachable vertex reachable, or\n  (b) is a forward-cross edge (u discovered before v, v not a descendant of u).\n- Delete u->v: the old forest is still a DFS forest unless u->v is a tree\n  edge (parent[v] == u), which dangles v's parent. A deleted non-tree edge\n  never creates a forward-cross edge, and every remaining vertex stays\n  reachable through its tree path (the tree is a subgraph of the graph).\n\nWhen the forest is affected we rebuild it from scratch (always correct); the\ncheap path is taken for the common case. The certificate the verifier reads\nis parent + discover + finish, with the no-forward-cross property.\n\"\"\"\n\nROOT = 0\n\n\ndef _dfs(graph, start, parent, discover, finish):\n    \"\"\"Iterative DFS over the reachable set from `start` in `graph`.\n\n    Fills parent/discover/finish for the newly reached vertices and returns\n    the set of vertices it visited. Neighbours are scanned in increasing\n    order, matching a standard recursive DFS.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(graph)\n    visited = set()\n    timer = [0]\n    stack = [(start, 0)]\n    parent[start] = None\n    discover[start] = 0\n    visited.add(start)\n    while stack:\n        u, idx = stack[-1]\n        row = graph[u]\n        advanced = False\n        while idx < n:\n            v = idx\n            idx += 1\n            if row[v] == 1 and v not in visited:\n                parent[v] = u\n                discover[v] = timer[0]\n                timer[0] += 1\n                visited.add(v)\n                stack[-1] = (u, idx)\n                stack.append((v, 0))\n                advanced = True\n                break\n        if not advanced:\n            finish[u] = timer[0]\n            timer[0] += 1\n            stack.pop()\n    return visited\n\n\ndef _rebuild(graph):\n    \"\"\"Full DFS forest of `graph` from the root.\"\"\"\n    n = len(graph)\n    parent = [None] * n\n    discover = [None] * n\n    finish = [None] * n\n    _dfs(graph, ROOT, parent, discover, finish)\n    return {\"parent\": parent, \"discover\": discover, \"finish\": finish}\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    return _rebuild(graph)\n\n\ndef _is_descendant(discover, finish, u, v):\n    \"\"\"True if v is a descendant of u (u discovered before v, v finished before u).\"\"\"\n    return discover[u] < discover[v] < finish[v] < finish[u]\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    parent = state[\"parent\"]\n    discover = state[\"discover\"]\n    finish = state[\"finish\"]\n\n    # (a) v becomes newly reachable: the old forest no longer spans the graph.\n    if discover[v] is None:\n        return _rebuild(graph)\n\n    # (b) u->v is a forward-cross edge: u discovered before v but v is not a\n    # descendant of u. (If v is an ancestor of u, the edge is a back edge, fine.)\n    if discover[u] < discover[v] and not _is_descendant(discover, finish, u, v):\n        return _rebuild(graph)\n\n    # Otherwise the old forest is still a valid DFS forest of the new graph.\n    return state\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    parent = state[\"parent\"]\n\n    # Only a deleted tree edge invalidates the forest (it dangles v's parent).\n    if v != ROOT and parent[v] == u:\n        return _rebuild(graph)\n\n    return state\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s2/candidate.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s2/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792508765947,"end":1792508765994}},"id":"prt_159d9102d0012dFh5Lk6NLOZyk","sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","messageID":"msg_159d90cf80015oGi2PyLyKCLJK"}}
