{"type":"text","timestamp":1792508788368,"sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","part":{"id":"prt_159d97276001hy1b5MawZXq36w","messageID":"msg_159d9500a001AKsSMOcFcbjUDV","sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","type":"text","text":"\n\nThe bug: `discover[u]` can be `None` when `u` is unreachable. I need to handle unreachable `u` (an edge from an unreachable `u` can't create a forward-cross edge, and can't make `v` newly reachable). Let me refine the logic to be both correct and avoid wasted rebuilds:\n\n","time":{"start":1792508785270,"end":1792508788362}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792508788422,"sessionID":"ses_ea62f61e9ffeZ6mYDjplW4oSwi","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bfd309536ded9f5a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_dfs_s2/candidate.py","oldString":"def insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    parent = state[\"parent\"]\n    discover = state[\"discover\"]\n    finish = state[\"finish\"]\n\n    # (a) v becomes newly reachable: the old forest no longer spans the graph.\n    if discover[v] is None:\n        return _rebuild(graph)\n\n    # (b) u->v is a forward-cross edge: u discovered before v but v is not a\n    # descendant of u. (If v is an ancestor of u, the edge is a back edge, fine.)\n    if discover[u] < discover[v] and not _is_descendant(discover, finish, u, v):\n        return _rebuild(graph)\n\n    # Otherwise the old forest is still a valid DFS forest of the new graph.\n    return state","newString":"def insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    parent = state[\"parent\"]\n    discover = state[\"discover\"]\n    finish = state[\"finish\"]\n\n    u_reach = discover[u] is not None\n    v_reach = discover[v] is not None\n\n    # (a) v becomes newly reachable (u reachable, v was not): the old forest\n    # no longer spans the reachable set.\n    if u_reach and not v_reach:\n        return _rebuild(graph)\n\n    # (b) u->v is a forward-cross edge: both reachable, u discovered before v,\n    # but v is not a descendant of u. (If v is an ancestor of u it is a back\n    # edge, fine; if u is unreachable the edge is not part of the forest.)\n    if (u_reach and v_reach and discover[u] < discover[v]\n            and not _is_descendant(discover, finish, u, v)):\n        return _rebuild(graph)\n\n    # Otherwise the old forest is still a valid DFS forest of the new graph.\n    return state"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/ethomdt/thesis/